1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,740
I'm on a journey out to see the world.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,700
While I'm on my own, I've
yet to reach the end.

3
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:09,420
So won't you come along with me right now?

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:13,420
Surely then we can!

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,780
Follow me now as we
journey on from sea to sea.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,220
For that treasure known
by everybody as one piece.

7
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,420
Even though they laugh and
say it's just a fantasy.

8
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,857
We are going, there's no doubt we go.

9
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,180
Cause we can feel the
rush of energy overcome.

10
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,280
It will lead the way.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:53,480
Keep pretending that you know what to do.

12
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:57,397
Books will only get in the way.

13
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,000
No guides for today.

14
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,977
Do not worry, soon the rain
will be gone with the wind.

15
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,597
Keep your chin up, raise the
anchor, now that's what you'll do.

16
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,257
Give it time and calm the storm
that you have built within.

17
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:11,417
Come and have my board at number two.

18
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,777
Once tomorrow's wind picks up,
we set self cause we can't.

19
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:17,277
Thresh enough, stand tall and
take a look at one of you.

20
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,657
All the journey makes
me wanna see somebody.

21
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,681
There are things out there
you just won't believe.

22
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,760
Beyond your wildest dreams.

23
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,297
Don't think for a second.

24
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:30,780
It's not the truth.

25
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,797
That's the story.

26
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,717
Most will believe.

27
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,037
Not me.

28
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,400
Come and see.

29
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,777
I am on a journey.

30
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,317
Out to see the world.

31
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,317
Don't all of my own.

32
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,317
I've got my group of friends.

33
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,357
Together we've got our way.

34
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,957
That's how it's done.

35
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,037
Says your captain.

36
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,277
Who says it can't be done.

37
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,937
We haven't even tried.

38
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,937
Gotta just believe we'll
make it to the end.

39
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,577
I just wanna do it all right now.

40
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,817
Together surely we can.

41
00:02:00,900 --> 00:02:02,717
Yes, we can.

42
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,117
You can.

43
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,757
Just take this moment in.

44
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,057
We can.

45
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,437
I can.

46
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,157
Just take this feeling in.

47
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,477
Right now.

48
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,900
Right now.

49
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:18,700
Oh yes, we can.

50
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:26,297
Yes, we can!

51
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,210
Yes, we can!

52
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:32,740
Edgy? Correct.

53
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:35,437
That's the sound that
Race makes when he runs.

54
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,638
Just another one of his many skills.

55
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,100
It's ninpo.

56
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:40,857
Blindfolding technique.

57
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:41,900
Now, guess who?

58
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,532
It's Kanjado, of course.

59
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:45,505
There's no one else behind me.

60
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:48,100
Hit the door!

61
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,680
Oh, you trickster, you!

62
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,520
He fell off!

63
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,960
What do we do now?

64
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,557
What was that thing, and why the
heck was it falling out of the sky?

65
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:05,470
I'm not sure.

66
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:06,737
At first glance,

67
00:03:06,820 --> 00:03:10,937
it looked like a wounded man covered
in blood and riddled with knives.

68
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,200
Or a little monkey.

69
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:15,257
You could have led with the
less gruesome one, you know!

70
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,297
Are you alive?

71
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:20,597
Say something back, are you alive?

72
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:24,477
Say something back—did they hit the water?

73
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:25,997
Let's save them, sir!

74
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,597
Loopy, not to worry—we are both unharmed!

75
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:31,017
Oh, that was kidding!

76
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,717
On, thank goodness—they're all right!

77
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,717
Please go on ahead—we'll reunite both!

78
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,997
Well, no way—is he crazy?

79
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:41,937
Let's turn around the
dragon—we need to go back!

80
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:43,397
Down—no other way! Hey,

81
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:47,937
turn around—he seems like he

82
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:53,377
wants to finish what

83
00:03:53,460 --> 00:04:00,460
he

84
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,610
started!

85
00:04:05,693 --> 00:04:06,617
No matter what he's
suffering—the better press on!

86
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,530
So cute!

87
00:04:07,613 --> 00:04:12,460
what he's suffering the
better press on so cute

88
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,480
Okay, we're going on ahead!

89
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,620
We'll see you guys there!

90
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:20,740
A valiant choice! Halt!

91
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:23,800
You're not welcome in
that country! Proceed!

92
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:28,320
Whoever that other guy is, he's not happy.

93
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,940
Stay strong, Ryunosuke!

94
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,600
You can do it.

95
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:51,650
Ouch!

96
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,220
I see the top!

97
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:58,780
Wow, we're so close!

98
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,780
You're in the home stretch now, big guy!

99
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:04,810
Sweet!

100
00:05:05,080 --> 00:05:06,580
Let's head to the top!

101
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:16,400
Come on!

102
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:18,305
Big sprint to the finish line!

103
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,720
Hey look!

104
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,077
I can see something!

105
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:44,940
A few more steps and we're there! Yeah!

106
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,450
Yeah!

107
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:52,223
Reunosuke!

108
00:05:52,306 --> 00:05:53,136
Be strong, Reunosuke.

109
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:55,080
Reunosuke!

110
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:56,960
Reunosuke!

111
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:59,577
Reunosuke! Reunosuke!

112
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:00,520
Reunosuke!

113
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,180
Eee?

114
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:04,960
We made it!

115
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,100
We're here!

116
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:08,840
We finally reached the top!

117
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:09,970
Reunosuke!

118
00:06:10,053 --> 00:06:11,840
It's all thanks to you!

119
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,540
We're on phone! Yeah!

120
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:23,240
Oh dear, you're changing back.

121
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,140
No, hold on!

122
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,250
Ryunosuke!

123
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,840
Ryunosuke! Don't go!

124
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,777
It's just a crappy drawing show.

125
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:56,117
Some respect, you jerks!

126
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,877
You can at least thank him
for bringing you all this way.

127
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,057
We don't know this place well.

128
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:02,497
Let's stay alert.

129
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:04,980
I mean, yeah, you're not wrong? but I...

130
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:08,840
Hey, Usopp, Ryunosuke was great, huh?

131
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:11,700
Never stop looking ahead. See that?

132
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,282
Must be the gate to the country.

133
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:18,188
Guess there really is a civilization
on this elephant's back.

134
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,700
They have a watchtower, but no guards.

135
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,120
Seems suspiciously undermanned.

136
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,440
Old business, aren't ya?

137
00:07:26,060 --> 00:07:29,217
How did you guys get over our
friend's death so quickly?

138
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:30,130
Jeez.

139
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:35,234
Usopp, get up here real quick
We can check out the view!

140
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:37,146
That's easier said than done!

141
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:40,540
After all that hard work, we're here!

142
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,560
We made it to ZO!

143
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:11,370
Whoa!

144
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,600
How is this real?

145
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:16,517
Now that we're up here, it's
just like any other country.

146
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,430
You're right.

147
00:08:17,513 --> 00:08:19,281
The whole thing is totally crazy.

148
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:22,657
Can you believe that elephant's
a thousand years old?

149
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,457
Let's explore. Come on.

150
00:08:24,540 --> 00:08:26,160
It'll be a blast. Uh-huh.

151
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:31,757
There's a forest and a
river and a town, too.

152
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,900
Yeah, it goes on as far
as the eye can see. Look!

153
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:37,081
That tree is shaped like a whale!

154
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:38,300
Whoa, it is!

155
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:40,599
That town is bigger than I thought!

156
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,250
Uh?

157
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,837
Wait, there's something
off about it, though.

158
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:45,750
Yeah!

159
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,820
Ah, there he goes again!

160
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:50,870
Typical.

161
00:08:50,953 --> 00:08:52,120
You see curly brows?

162
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,860
Nope, I'm too high up to see anyone!

163
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:58,768
Zoro, should we wait
here for the other two?

164
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,060
Nah, this place isn't that big.

165
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:03,120
They'll find us.

166
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,700
Don't just run off.

167
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:05,750
I'm coming too.

168
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:08,260
Why'd he jump the gates wide open?

169
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,857
That's not how I'd describe it.

170
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,377
Yeah, it was destroyed by force.

171
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,360
See, they plowed right through

172
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:25,370
it.

173
00:09:25,453 --> 00:09:26,283
Not just that.

174
00:09:26,366 --> 00:09:27,337
Look at the trail too.

175
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:30,361
No normal animal could
have made a path this wide.

176
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:34,060
You're right, man.

177
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:36,257
This is some next-level destruction.

178
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:37,634
It's still fresh, too.

179
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:39,469
Hope Sanji's group's okay.

180
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,560
Huh? What the heck?

181
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:45,197
It didn't look like this
from the watchtower.

182
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,097
What could have made this mess?

183
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,020
Only one way to find out.

184
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:50,857
We haven't even met the people here.

185
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:53,646
We've already got some
monster to worry about.

186
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,060
Wait, slow down.

187
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:58,677
If you guys would listen to me once in
a while and run away from the bad stuff,

188
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,642
our lives would be a lot better.

189
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:06,000
This is hard to walk on.

190
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:07,711
Yeah, it's elephant skin.

191
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:10,900
The flowers here grow in odd places.

192
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,080
What happened to Part?

193
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:16,197
The lesser minks waltz
right through the gate.

194
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,580
Maybe they beat him.

195
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,020
Whoa, this feels so weird!

196
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:22,480
It's really soft under your feet!

197
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:25,060
Here's the town!

198
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,257
There's tons of buildings,
but I don't see anybody!

199
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,860
Where are all the people?

200
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:38,440
Hey, Sanji, Nami, Chopper, Brock, Momo,
are any of you guys around? Where are you?

201
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:40,760
Come on, answer me! Hello?

202
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,599
Whoops, I forgot the gas guy again.

203
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:47,060
Jeez, what happened here?

204
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:49,324
Is that gunpowder I'm smelling?

205
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:51,797
Yeah, and a little bit of gas, too.

206
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:52,710
Oh, great.

207
00:10:52,793 --> 00:10:53,623
More trouble.

208
00:10:53,706 --> 00:10:55,897
Can't we just go to a peaceful
island once in a while?

209
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:56,940
I mean, really.

210
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,200
Ah, what's up? What'd you see?

211
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,520
I got this.

212
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:08,800
She just jumped.

213
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,340
In mid-air.

214
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,220
What the?

215
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:17,050
Catch!

216
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,160
Stop immediately!

217
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:26,640
Forget about them! We must go!

218
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:29,680
The whale forest has been invaded.

219
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:32,980
Talking animals?

220
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,540
There's a mink tribe.

221
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:40,480
Hey, I know those clothes.

222
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:44,520
But that's not Nami.

223
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,557
Damn, what the hell is that weapon?

224
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:57,860
That thing gave me a serious shock.

225
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,137
There's an invader in the Will Force, too?

226
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,040
Yes, the situation is dire.

227
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,357
The Guardians are not going
to be happy about this.

228
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,460
What is she?

229
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:08,720
Some kind of dog? Listen,

230
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:12,277
you better tell us where you got that
outfit because it doesn't belong to you.

231
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,200
What did you do, Nutanami?

232
00:12:14,660 --> 00:12:17,240
Do you think they're cannibals? Great!

233
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,794
No, I'm double scared!

234
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,250
Ah!

235
00:12:21,380 --> 00:12:23,439
Oh, please don't eat me, nice lady!

236
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,800
Whoa, talk about air!

237
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:29,515
Man, do all of these mink
people have skills like that?

238
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,410
Carrot!

239
00:12:34,493 --> 00:12:35,595
See anything unusual?

240
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:41,890
Over there!

241
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,924
I just hope we're not too late!

242
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:48,057
It's in the whale forest on
the other side of Karoo City!

243
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,040
I thought so.

244
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:50,680
Let's go, Warnie!

245
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:54,660
Now! Get on!

246
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:56,010
Right!

247
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:59,195
There's no time to transport you, Tia.

248
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,322
Listen closely.

249
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:04,797
All of you should head to the west,
by way of the right-trump forest.

250
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:08,762
And then, if you turn left at the
swamp, you'll reach right flank.

251
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,748
That's where you'll
find your cruise corpse.

252
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:14,500
We'll find what?!

253
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,308
Wait for us in right flank!

254
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,205
We'll catch up to you shortly!

255
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,216
I wonder if they're going to be okay.

256
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,936
That group was the Straw Hat Pirates.

257
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,160
Is that true?

258
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,067
They're in for a real shock.

259
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:36,477
We don't have time to
deal with them right now.

260
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:37,972
This is far more urgent.

261
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,997
Since the rest of the crew
has finally showed up,

262
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:44,697
I assume that the invader in the
Whale Forest is Straw Hat Luffy.

263
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,780
And while he may be their captain,

264
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,394
the Guardians won't show him any mercy.

265
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,666
The rest of the crew is dead!

266
00:13:56,340 --> 00:14:00,693
Well, she did say that there was a
corpse, which means they weren't eaten.

267
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:01,957
That's not the point!

268
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,640
Stop being so morbid!

269
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:07,837
That's enough crying.

270
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,155
Nobody's been killed.

271
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:11,798
Curly Browse is with them, remember?

272
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,420
Yeah, Zorro's right.

273
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:16,217
There's no way they would
go down that easily.

274
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:19,497
Those animal ladies must be
trying to trick us somehow.

275
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:22,380
Probably so, but what a terrible lie.

276
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:28,140
Tell me, the rest of your crewmates,
they should be here, correct? Uh-huh.

277
00:14:28,560 --> 00:14:29,937
And can you contact them?

278
00:14:30,020 --> 00:14:30,902
I'm afraid not.

279
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:34,200
I didn't even really expect
I would see them again.

280
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,277
Actually, hold on.

281
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:38,280
Almost forgot.

282
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,160
I still have a Vever card.

283
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:42,730
See this?

284
00:14:42,813 --> 00:14:44,620
It's for our navigator, Beppo.

285
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:47,897
Oh, yeah, the talking polar bear, right?

286
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,745
I guess he's a mink, isn't he?

287
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:54,060
Yeah, this place is where he was born.

288
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:56,910
However,

289
00:14:57,020 --> 00:14:59,057
he left the island when
he was a little boy,

290
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:03,557
so he doesn't remember much about living
here or being part of the mink tribe.

291
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:05,640
I've known him for a whole decade.

292
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:06,660
He's a friend.

293
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:10,460
So if you want reliable info, follow me.

294
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,660
Wait, there's a town that way, you guys.

295
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:16,897
I remember seeing it from the tower.

296
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:18,797
I mean, who knows what we'll run into?

297
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,100
It's not safe!

298
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:21,947
We might see some cannibals.

299
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,777
It's better than trusting
what that dog lady said.

300
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,377
I think we should follow him.

301
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,290
Come on.

302
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,180
Gum-Gum!

303
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:43,450
Mugolaba!

304
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:51,190
What's wrong?

305
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,740
It doesn't make sense!

306
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,797
His Electro isn't working at all!

307
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:55,710
Wait, you two!

308
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,420
Please stop attacking him!

309
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,700
It's fine, he's somebody I know!

310
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:02,079
Either way, he's still an intruder!

311
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:05,851
If he won't stop, then I'm
afraid I'll have to force you...

312
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,340
...out of our way!

313
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:10,510
Oh, no!

314
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:11,700
Parshat Bart!

315
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:14,297
I don't think we can handle this guy.

316
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:15,957
You're right, he's way too tough.

317
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:18,280
Donnie, stop this! That's enough!

318
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:19,638
Look what I've got!

319
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,040
How about a banana?

320
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,180
Lucky me!

321
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:53,180
That's one way to do it.

322
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,430
Dog?

323
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:05,740
Yutia must be Straw Hat Luffy.

324
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:07,540
My name is Wanda,

325
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,840
and this is Carrot.

326
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:13,760
We'll do you no harm.

327
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:15,561
So don't resist.

328
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:18,480
This place is full of talking animals.

329
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:21,231
It's like a whole island full of choppers.

330
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,020
What's up with these two?

331
00:17:23,320 --> 00:17:25,580
They came and jumped me for no reason.

332
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:29,513
That's because your kind is
forbidden to enter this area.

333
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,380
Whoa, back up.

334
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:33,900
Guardians, please.

335
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:35,760
Forget this man.

336
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:37,560
We'll take him.

337
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,440
Fine, for Wanda's sake.

338
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,720
Retreat, Roddy!

339
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,400
Be me!

340
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:53,840
It's Pedro.

341
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,900
Everyone, out!

342
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,940
I didn't even notice they were here!

343
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:09,760
Be grateful Yutia didn't encounter
them on a moonlit night. Strawhead!

344
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,590
Oh, come on!

345
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:16,457
Why do you look so confused?

346
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,817
Don't you remember us?

347
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:21,097
We took care of you after what
happened back in Marineford!

348
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:23,760
How could you forget that? Oh, yeah!

349
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:24,900
I know you!

350
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:28,137
You're the talking bear who was
part of Traffy's crew, right?

351
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:29,060
Who's Traffy?

352
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:32,600
Listen, our captain is the
genius surgeon Trafalgar Law!

353
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:35,600
We're the heart pirates, okay? I know.

354
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:36,978
That's what I said.

355
00:18:37,140 --> 00:18:38,316
Don't start with me!

356
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,780
So, we've kept up with the news.

357
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,417
So much has been happening.

358
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:44,520
Guess we're allies now, huh?

359
00:18:44,860 --> 00:18:46,840
Is our captain here? Uh-huh.

360
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,417
Jeffy's here with us.

361
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:49,857
You keep saying that name!

362
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:51,620
Who is that? Aye-aye!

363
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:53,900
That's what I call law.

364
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,180
Oh, really?

365
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,480
That wasn't clear.

366
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:59,797
Well, whatever, I'm just glad
to hear he's on the island.

367
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,480
Yeah, I can't wait to
see our captain again!

368
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:11,080
There's no doubting it.

369
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:12,573
This city was attacked.

370
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:18,153
Judging by the size, the population
could be in the hundreds of thousands.

371
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,540
But I don't see a single resident.

372
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:25,537
If we stay out here in the open,
they'll come and get us for sure!

373
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:27,757
They're probably still
around here, aren't they?

374
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:29,193
We gotta run for cover!

375
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,150
Let's hurry!

376
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,538
Is that some kind of torture device?

377
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:40,537
Kind of hard to say whether we're dealing
with humans or something else here

378
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:43,177
I don't know, but they're
all over the place.

379
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:46,040
Must be something pretty
strong to do that.

380
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,300
Hey, check this out.

381
00:19:53,680 --> 00:19:55,798
I think it's some kind of footprint.

382
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:58,720
Another elephant, maybe?

383
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:00,760
Yeah, everything's bad.

384
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,957
I say we just...

385
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:07,400
There were claw marks, so it
could have been infighting.

386
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,875
We do know one thing.

387
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,100
This place fell, but it
hasn't been that long.

388
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,760
Two weeks, maybe less.

389
00:20:20,020 --> 00:20:21,280
Wait, really?

390
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:27,360
If that's true, then this city got
wrecked while our friends were here!

391
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:33,460
Oh, so that's why there's nobody around.

392
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:37,137
The country's history
goes back for centuries.

393
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:39,660
It's called the Mokumo Dukedom.

394
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:44,849
It was only half a month ago that I
could still see everyone's smiling faces.

395
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:58,160
The name of the man who caused
all this suffering is Jack.

396
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,590
Whoa!

397
00:21:02,673 --> 00:21:03,820
Now what's up?

398
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:08,100
Is this something bad?
Hooray! Inruption's coming!

399
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:09,760
I'm on the train!

400
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,660
Get a lorny!

401
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:14,509
We'll head to right flank!

402
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:16,544
Your friends are waiting there!

403
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:17,830
Oh sweet!

404
00:21:17,920 --> 00:21:19,685
You mean Sanji's group, right?

405
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:21,890
Hello?
